{% extends "tutorial_base.html.j2" %}

{% block tutorial_body %}
        <!-- Intro Card -->
        <div class="doc-intro-card">
          <h2>Why You Need Motion-Synchronized Torch Control in SimCNC</h2>
          <p>
            Stock SimCNC fires and stops your torch with macro calls (<code class="mono">d.setSpindleState()</code> / <code class="mono">d.setThcState()</code>) and velocity-zero stalls (<code class="mono">d.waitForZeroVelocity()</code>). Your machine must come to a full stop before the arc shuts off.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
            That stop-and-wait delay makes <strong>Zero-Overburn Early Torch-Out</strong> and <strong>3D Ramp Lead-Ins (Flying Pierce)</strong> impossible without burning a divot into your tube wall. Make these three updates across <code class="mono">config.xml</code>, <code class="mono">___CONF.py</code>, <code class="mono">m3.py</code>, <code class="mono">m5.py</code>, and your G-code output:
          </p>

          <ul class="doc-bullet-list" style="margin-top: 0.85rem;">
            <li>
              <strong>1. Trajectory Sync Outputs (<code class="mono">ExtTrajSyncOut1 / P1</code> &amp; <code class="mono">ExtTrajSyncOut0 / P0</code>):</strong>
              Move your <strong>Torch Fire Relay (<code class="mono">Output 0</code>)</strong> and <strong>Hardware THC Lock (<code class="mono">Output 4</code>)</strong> to SimCNC's trajectory sync channels. Your G-code switches them inside the motion planner with <code class="mono">M62 P&lt;n&gt;</code> (<code class="mono">ON</code>) and <code class="mono">M63 P&lt;n&gt;</code> (<code class="mono">OFF</code>).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>2. Direct <code class="mono">Arc OK</code> Hardware Polling (<code class="mono">Digital Input 0</code>):</strong>
              Read the isolated <code class="mono">Arc OK</code> signal straight from CSMIO/IP-M <code class="mono">Digital Input 0</code>. You skip SimCNC's software THC state machine (<code class="mono">#4071</code>) completely.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>3. Stationary Micro-Wiggle (<code class="mono">&lt;1.5 ms</code>):</strong>
              SimCNC blocks <code class="mono">mod.setDigitalIO()</code> on <code class="mono">ExtTrajSyncOut</code> pins, and <code class="mono">M62</code>/<code class="mono">M63</code> only fire during motion. While stationary, <code class="mono">m3.py</code> and <code class="mono">m5.py</code> run a zero-net Z micro-wiggle (<code class="mono">±0.0005"</code> / <code class="mono">±0.01 mm</code>) right after <code class="mono">M62</code>/<code class="mono">M63</code> to trip the relay in <code class="mono">&lt;1.5 ms</code>. Mid-cut, <code class="mono">M63 P1</code> before a lead-out shuts the arc off on the fly at full speed.
            </li>
          </ul>

          <div class="doc-intro-grid">
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Torch Fire Relay (P1)</span>
              <span class="value"><code class="mono">ExtTrajSyncOut1</code> → Output 0 (<code class="mono">M62/M63 P1</code>)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Hardware THC Lock (P0)</span>
              <span class="value"><code class="mono">ExtTrajSyncOut0</code> → Output 4 (<code class="mono">M62/M63 P0</code>)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Direct Arc OK Input</span>
              <span class="value">CSMIO/IP-M Digital Input 0 (<code class="mono">5 ms</code> Poll)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             PART I BANNER
             ================================================================== -->
        <div class="doc-section-divider" id="part-1">
          <div class="doc-section-kicker">Part I • Real-Time Trajectory I/O Synchronization</div>
          <h2 class="doc-section-heading">Step-by-Step Setup: Motion-Synchronized Torch On/Off</h2>
          <p class="doc-section-desc">
            Update <code class="mono">config.xml</code>, <code class="mono">___CONF.py</code>, <code class="mono">m3.py</code>, and <code class="mono">m5.py</code> so your torch relay and THC lock switch in lockstep with <code class="mono">M62</code>/<code class="mono">M63</code> moves.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 1
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-1">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 01</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Unassign Legacy Spindle &amp; Software THC Outputs in <code class="mono">config.xml</code></h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              SimCNC will not share an output pin between <code class="mono">SpindleCW</code> / software THC and <code class="mono">ExtTrajSyncOut</code>. Clear your old pin mappings first:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>
                <strong>1. Unassign Spindle CW Output:</strong> Open <span class="ui-chip">Configuration → Settings → Spindle</span> (<code class="mono">config.xml:2629-2643</code>). Set <code class="mono">&lt;spindleCwIOSignal&gt;</code> to <code class="mono">&lt;moduleIndex&gt;-1&lt;/moduleIndex&gt;</code> and <code class="mono">&lt;pinNr&gt;-1&lt;/pinNr&gt;</code>.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>2. Unassign Software THC Pins:</strong> Open <span class="ui-chip">Configuration → Settings → THC</span> (<code class="mono">config.xml:4327-4371</code>). Leave <code class="mono">&lt;THCUp&gt;</code>, <code class="mono">&lt;THCDown&gt;</code>, and <code class="mono">&lt;THCTorchOnDigital&gt;</code> set to <code class="mono">pinNr = -1</code>. Your external hardware THC and direct <code class="mono">Arc OK</code> line will run with zero software interference.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot"></span> config.xml (Lines 2629–2643 &amp; 4327–4371): Unassigned Spindle &amp; Software THC</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">XML</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>&lt;!-- Configuration → Settings → Spindle (config.xml:2629-2643) --&gt;
&lt;spindleCwIOSignal&gt;
 &lt;ioPinDescriptor&gt;
  &lt;IOPortDescriptor&gt;
   &lt;ModuleDescriptor&gt;
    &lt;moduleType&gt;IP&lt;/moduleType&gt;
    &lt;moduleIndex&gt;-1&lt;/moduleIndex&gt;
   &lt;/ModuleDescriptor&gt;
   &lt;ioPortType&gt;DIGITAL&lt;/ioPortType&gt;
   &lt;ioPortDirection&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/ioPortDirection&gt;
  &lt;/IOPortDescriptor&gt;
  &lt;pinNr&gt;-1&lt;/pinNr&gt;
 &lt;/ioPinDescriptor&gt;
 &lt;inverted&gt;false&lt;/inverted&gt;
&lt;/spindleCwIOSignal&gt;</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 2
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-2">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 02</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Assign Physical Outputs to <code class="mono">ExternalTrajCtrl</code> in <code class="mono">config.xml</code></h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Map your CSMIO/IP-M digital outputs under <span class="ui-chip">Configuration → Settings → Special IO</span> (<code class="mono">&lt;axesManager&gt;&lt;ExternalTrajCtrl&gt;</code> at <code class="mono">config.xml:5046-5074</code>):
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>
                <strong><code class="mono">ExtTrajSyncOut0</code> (<code class="mono">P0</code>: Hardware THC Lock/Enable):</strong> → CSMIO/IP Module <code class="mono">0</code>, Digital <code class="mono">OUTPUT</code>, Pin <code class="mono">4</code> (<code class="mono">config.xml:5047-5060</code>).
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong><code class="mono">ExtTrajSyncOut1</code> (<code class="mono">P1</code>: Plasma Torch Fire Relay):</strong> → CSMIO/IP Module <code class="mono">0</code>, Digital <code class="mono">OUTPUT</code>, Pin <code class="mono">0</code> (<code class="mono">config.xml:5061-5074</code>).
              </li>
            </ul>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot cyan"></span> config.xml (Lines 5046–5074): &lt;axesManager&gt;&lt;ExternalTrajCtrl&gt;</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">XML</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>&lt;ExternalTrajCtrl&gt;
 &lt;ExtTrajSyncOut0&gt;
  &lt;ioPinDescriptor&gt;
   &lt;IOPortDescriptor&gt;
    &lt;ModuleDescriptor&gt;
     &lt;moduleType&gt;IP&lt;/moduleType&gt;
     &lt;moduleIndex&gt;0&lt;/moduleIndex&gt;
    &lt;/ModuleDescriptor&gt;
    &lt;ioPortType&gt;DIGITAL&lt;/ioPortType&gt;
    &lt;ioPortDirection&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/ioPortDirection&gt;
   &lt;/IOPortDescriptor&gt;
   &lt;pinNr&gt;4&lt;/pinNr&gt;
  &lt;/ioPinDescriptor&gt;
  &lt;inverted&gt;false&lt;/inverted&gt;
 &lt;/ExtTrajSyncOut0&gt;
 &lt;ExtTrajSyncOut1&gt;
  &lt;ioPinDescriptor&gt;
   &lt;IOPortDescriptor&gt;
    &lt;ModuleDescriptor&gt;
     &lt;moduleType&gt;IP&lt;/moduleType&gt;
     &lt;moduleIndex&gt;0&lt;/moduleIndex&gt;
    &lt;/ModuleDescriptor&gt;
    &lt;ioPortType&gt;DIGITAL&lt;/ioPortType&gt;
    &lt;ioPortDirection&gt;OUTPUT&lt;/ioPortDirection&gt;
   &lt;/IOPortDescriptor&gt;
   &lt;pinNr&gt;0&lt;/pinNr&gt;
  &lt;/ioPinDescriptor&gt;
  &lt;inverted&gt;false&lt;/inverted&gt;
 &lt;/ExtTrajSyncOut1&gt;
&lt;/ExternalTrajCtrl&gt;</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 3
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-3">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 03</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Create Trajectory-Sync &amp; Hardware Arc-OK Helpers in <code class="mono">___CONF.py</code></h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Add these shared helpers to <code class="mono">___CONF.py</code> and import them (<code class="mono">from ___CONF import *</code>) in <code class="mono">m3.py:7</code> and <code class="mono">m5.py:5</code>:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>
                <strong>1. Pin Constants (<code class="mono">___CONF.py:4-23</code>):</strong>
                <code class="mono">THC_Sync_Pin = "P0"</code> (Output 4), <code class="mono">Arc_Sync_Pin = "P1"</code> (Output 0), and <code class="mono">Arc_OK_Pin = 0</code> with <code class="mono">Arc_OK_Inverted = True</code> (active-low <code class="mono">DIOPinVal.PinReset</code> when cutting).
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>2. Stationary Micro-Wiggle Helpers:</strong>
                <code class="mono">fire_torch_hardware()</code> and <code class="mono">extinguish_torch_hardware()</code> queue <code class="mono">M62</code>/<code class="mono">M63</code> plus a <code class="mono">G91</code> Z wiggle (<code class="mono">±0.0005"</code> at <code class="mono">F100.0</code> or <code class="mono">±0.01 mm</code> at <code class="mono">F2500.0</code>) in one <code class="mono">d.executeGCodeList()</code> call. Sending one list avoids UDP lag and flips the relay in <code class="mono">&lt;1.5 ms</code>.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>3. Direct Hardware Arc OK Check (<code class="mono">check_arc_ok()</code>):</strong>
                Reads <code class="mono">Digital Input 0</code> straight from <code class="mono">ModuleType.IP, 0</code> instead of polling parameter <code class="mono">#4071</code>.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot emerald"></span> ___CONF.py: Trajectory-Sync &amp; Direct Hardware Arc-OK Helpers</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">PYTHON</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code># ___CONF.py: Shared Hardware Trajectory Sync &amp; Direct Arc-OK Helpers
THC_Sync_Pin = "P0"      # ExtTrajSyncOut0 -&gt; CSMIO/IP-M Digital Output 4 (Hardware THC Lock)
Arc_Sync_Pin = "P1"      # ExtTrajSyncOut1 -&gt; CSMIO/IP-M Digital Output 0 (Plasma Torch Fire Relay)

Arc_OK_Pin = 0           # CSMIO/IP-M Digital Input 0 (Optically Isolated Arc OK)
Arc_OK_Inverted = True   # Active-low: DIOPinVal.PinReset when plasma arc is conducting


def _wiggle_params(d):
    """Return zero-net-displacement Z micro-wiggle step and feedrate for current machine units."""
    try:
        is_inch = ("inch" in gui.edPlasmaUnits.getText().lower())
    except Exception:
        is_inch = False
    if is_inch:
        return ("0.0005", "100.0")
    return ("0.01", "2500.0")


def trigger_motion_sync(d):
    """Execute a zero-net-displacement Z micro-wiggle to flush pending M62/M63 pins while stationary."""
    step, feed = _wiggle_params(d)
    d.executeGCodeList([
        "G91",
        f"G1 Z{step} F{feed}",
        f"G1 Z-{step} F{feed}",
        "G90"
    ])


def fire_torch_hardware(d):
    """Latch ExtTrajSyncOut1 (Output 0) ON while stationary in &lt;1.5ms via single G-code list."""
    step, feed = _wiggle_params(d)
    d.executeGCodeList([
        f"M62 {Arc_Sync_Pin}",
        "G91",
        f"G1 Z{step} F{feed}",
        f"G1 Z-{step} F{feed}",
        "G90"
    ])


def extinguish_torch_hardware(d):
    """Clear Torch Relay (P1) and lock THC (P0) while stationary via single G-code list."""
    step, feed = _wiggle_params(d)
    d.executeGCodeList([
        f"M63 {Arc_Sync_Pin}",
        f"M63 {THC_Sync_Pin}",
        "G91",
        f"G1 Z{step} F{feed}",
        f"G1 Z-{step} F{feed}",
        "G90"
    ])


def check_arc_ok(d):
    """Read optically isolated Arc OK input directly from CSMIO/IP-M Module 0 Digital Input 0."""
    mod = d.getModule(ModuleType.IP, 0)
    pin_state = mod.getDigitalIO(IOPortDir.InputPort, Arc_OK_Pin)
    if Arc_OK_Inverted:
        return (pin_state == DIOPinVal.PinReset)
    return (pin_state == DIOPinVal.PinSet)</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 4
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-4">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 04</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Update <code class="mono">m3.py</code> for Synchronized Ignition &amp; Ramp Lead-In</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Update your <code class="mono">m3.py</code> macro in four spots:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>
                <strong>1. Pre-Cut Reset (<code class="mono">m3.py:231-260</code>):</strong>
                Replace stock <code class="mono">d.setSpindleState(SpindleState.OFF)</code> / <code class="mono">d.setThcState(ThcState.Off)</code> loops with <code class="mono">d.executeGCode("M63 P0")</code> and <code class="mono">extinguish_torch_hardware(d)</code>. Poll <code class="mono">while check_arc_ok(d):</code> before probing so you never touch off on a live arc.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>2. Pre-Fire Check &amp; Ignition (<code class="mono">m3.py:500-519</code>):</strong>
                At <code class="mono">Pierce_height</code>, check <code class="mono">if check_arc_ok(d): emergency(...)</code> to catch shorted wiring. Then call <code class="mono">fire_torch_hardware(d)</code> to close <code class="mono">Output 0</code>.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>3. Direct 5 ms Arc OK Polling (<code class="mono">m3.py:523-602</code>):</strong>
                Swap <code class="mono">#4071</code> checks for <code class="mono">while not check_arc_ok(d):</code> with <code class="mono">time.sleep(0.005)</code> during arc transfer and pierce delay.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>4. 3D Ramp Handoff &amp; Stall Removal (<code class="mono">m3.py:604-626</code>):</strong>
                When <code class="mono">#1113 == 1.0</code>, leave Z at <code class="mono">Pierce_height</code> and reset <code class="mono">#1113</code> to <code class="mono">0.0</code> so the next lead-in ramps down in motion. Delete <code class="mono">d.waitForZeroVelocity(0.1)</code> and <code class="mono">d.setThcState(ThcState.On)</code> at the end of <code class="mono">m3.py</code>; G-code handles THC lock via <code class="mono">M62 P0</code> / <code class="mono">M63 P0</code>.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot"></span> m3.py: Synchronized Torch Ignition, 5ms Arc-OK Poll &amp; Stall-Free Exit</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">PYTHON</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>from ___CONF import *

# 1. Pre-Fire Fault Check &amp; Synchronized Torch Fire (m3.py:500-519)
if check_arc_ok(d):
    emergency("Arc OK signal active before firing torch; check wiring!")

fire_torch_hardware(d)  # Executes M62 P1 + Z micro-wiggle to close Output 0 in &lt;1.5ms

# 2. Direct Hardware Arc Transfer Poll at 5ms intervals (m3.py:523-542)
max_transfer_time = time.time() + Ignition_timeout
while not check_arc_ok(d):
    if time.time() &gt; max_transfer_time:
        extinguish_torch_hardware(d)
        emergency("Arc transfer timeout: no Arc OK signal received")
    time.sleep(0.005)

# ... (See Part II below for Two-Tier Pierce Dwell &amp; #1113 3D Ramp Handoff) ...
# NOTE: Do NOT call d.waitForZeroVelocity(0.1) or d.setThcState(ThcState.On) at the end of m3.py!</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 5
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-5">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 05</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Update <code class="mono">m5.py</code> for Dual-Path Arc Extinguish</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Replace stock <code class="mono">m5.py</code> with this two-path check so mid-motion torch stops retract immediately with zero pause:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>
                <strong>1. Arc Still Active (<code class="mono">m5.py:54-63</code>):</strong>
                On an open path or manual stop, <code class="mono">check_arc_ok(d)</code> returns <code class="mono">True</code>. <code class="mono">extinguish_torch_hardware(d)</code> clears <code class="mono">P1</code> and <code class="mono">P0</code> with a Z wiggle, then waits up to <code class="mono">0.5 s</code> for <code class="mono">Arc OK</code> to drop.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>2. Arc Already Out (<code class="mono">m5.py:64-75</code>):</strong>
                When <code class="mono">M63 P1</code> already fired on a lead-out or overburn move, <code class="mono">check_arc_ok(d)</code> is <code class="mono">False</code>. <code class="mono">m5.py</code> skips both the Z wiggle and stock <code class="mono">d.waitForZeroVelocity(1)</code> stall, cleans up <code class="mono">P1</code>/<code class="mono">P0</code>, and retracts straight to Safe Z.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot cyan"></span> m5.py (Lines 51–75): Dual-Path Stationary vs. On-The-Fly Arc Extinguish</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">PYTHON</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>from ___CONF import *

# 1. Check Live Hardware Arc State (m5.py:51-52)
arc_active = check_arc_ok(d)

if arc_active:
    # Branch 1: Arc still active (stationary stop) -> single M63 P1 + M63 P0 + Z micro-wiggle list
    extinguish_torch_hardware(d)
    t_timeout = time.time() + 0.5
    while check_arc_ok(d) and time.time() &lt; t_timeout:
        time.sleep(0.005)
else:
    # Branch 2: Arc already extinguished on-the-fly by M63 P1 during lead-out / overburn!
    # Skip Z micro-wiggle &amp; skip waitForZeroVelocity(1) for instant retract to Safe Z
    d.executeGCode(f"M63 {Arc_Sync_Pin}")
    d.executeGCode(f"M63 {THC_Sync_Pin}")

d.setSpindleState(SpindleState.OFF)</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 6
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-6">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 06</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Emit Synchronized <code class="mono">M62</code>/<code class="mono">M63</code> in G-Code (RotaryCAM Post-Processor)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              With SimCNC wired for trajectory sync, your posted G-code coordinates <code class="mono">P0</code> (THC Lock) and <code class="mono">P1</code> (Torch Relay) inline with every cut:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>
                <strong>1. Cut Start:</strong> Emits <code class="mono">M3</code> so <code class="mono">m3.py</code> probes, fires via <code class="mono">M62 P1</code> + wiggle, and dwells (or emits <code class="mono">M62 P1</code> before lead-in when <code class="mono">useM3M5</code> is off).
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>2. THC Lock (<code class="mono">P0</code>):</strong> Emits <code class="mono">M63 P0</code> before HSS tube corners, small holes, and lead-outs, then unlocks with <code class="mono">M62 P0</code> at steady cutting speed.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>3. Zero-Overburn Early Torch-Out (<code class="mono">P1</code>):</strong> Right before the lead-out or overburn <code class="mono">G1</code>/<code class="mono">G2</code>/<code class="mono">G3</code> move, your G-code emits <code class="mono">M63 P0</code> (stops THC dive on voltage drop) and <code class="mono">M63 P1</code> (kills the torch on the first motion step), followed by <code class="mono">M5</code>.
              </li>
            </ul>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot emerald"></span> RotaryCAM Post-Processor Output: Zero-Overburn Early Torch-Out Sequence</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">G-CODE</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>( --- ACTIVE CONTOUR CUTTING WITH HARDWARE THC UNLOCKED --- )
M62 P0                          ( Unlock Hardware THC at steady surface speed )
G1 X48.320 Y0.000 Z13.500 A264.200 F2200.0

( --- ZERO-OVERBURN EARLY TORCH-OUT ON LEAD-OUT / OVERBURN --- )
M63 P0                          ( 1. Lock Hardware THC before arc voltage decays )
M63 P1                          ( 2. Arm Torch Relay OFF on first step of overburn move )
G1 X48.350 Y0.000 Z13.500 A267.500 F2200.0   ( Torch extinguishes in motion across seam )
M5                              ( 3. Fast no-wiggle cleanup &amp; immediate Safe Z retract )</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="doc-callout info" style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
              <div class="doc-callout-title">🛡 SimCNC 3.6+ (<code class="mono">G93</code> Inverse-Time) Controller-Safe Hardening</div>
              <p>
                When you run the <strong>SimCNC 3.6+ (<code class="mono">G93</code> Inverse-Time)</strong> profile, your <code class="mono">G21</code> metric and <code class="mono">G20</code> inch code follows these safety rules automatically:
              </p>
              <ul class="doc-bullet-list" style="margin-top: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
                <li><strong>Smooth Blending:</strong> Emits <code class="mono">G69</code> and metric <code class="mono">G64 P0.3</code>/<code class="mono">P0.4</code> even inside <code class="mono">G20</code> inch programs, never <code class="mono">G61</code> exact-stop.</li>
                <li><strong>G93 Feed Floor:</strong> Formats <code class="mono">G93 F</code> to <code class="mono">4</code> decimals with a <code class="mono">0.0001</code> floor.</li>
                <li><strong>Sliver &amp; Dwell Cleanup:</strong> Merges <code class="mono">&lt; 0.05 mm</code> / <code class="mono">&lt; 0.02&deg;</code> micro-moves, feathers pure-XYZ to pure-ABC transitions by <code class="mono">0.002 mm</code> (<code class="mono">0.0026 mm</code> in <code class="mono">G20</code>), and drops sub-<code class="mono">1 ms</code> dwells (<code class="mono">G4 P&ge;1</code> ms).</li>
                <li><strong>Comments &amp; Parameters:</strong> Keeps one <code class="mono">(...)</code> comment per line and stays under <code class="mono">#1999</code> (with <code class="mono">#4061</code> THC allowlist and <code class="mono">G4 P1</code> sync).</li>
                <li><strong>Clean Arcs &amp; Rotary Unwinds:</strong> Outputs <code class="mono">5</code>-decimal <code class="mono">G20</code> arcs (<code class="mono">I/J/K</code> within <code class="mono">0.005 mm</code>, split full circles, no <code class="mono">G90.1</code>/<code class="mono">G91.1</code>) plus <code class="mono">G92 A</code> unwinds (no <code class="mono">G92.1</code>, explicit <code class="mono">G0</code>/<code class="mono">G1</code> after <code class="mono">G80</code>).</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             PART II BANNER: 3D RAMP LEAD-INS
             ================================================================== -->
        <div class="doc-section-divider cyan" id="part-2">
          <div class="doc-section-kicker">Part II • Parameter Handshake (#1113 / #1110 / Z#3)</div>
          <h2 class="doc-section-heading">How 3D Ramp Lead-Ins Work in <code class="mono">m3.py</code> &amp; G-Code</h2>
          <p class="doc-section-desc">
            Swap stationary vertical plunges for a coordinated 3D ramp from <code class="mono">Pierce_height (#2)</code> down to <code class="mono">Cut_height (#3)</code> along your lead-in path.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Overview Card for Part II -->
        <div class="doc-intro-card" id="ramp-overview">
          <h2>Three-Parameter Handshake Between G-Code and <code class="mono">m3.py</code></h2>
          <p>
            Stock <code class="mono">m3.py:190-205</code> fires at <code class="mono">Pierce_height (#2)</code>, waits <code class="mono">100%</code> of <code class="mono">Pierce_delay (#4)</code>, and plunges straight down into molten slag before moving XY. A 3D ramp lead-in descends in <code class="mono">X + Y + Z (+ A)</code> along the lead-in line or helical arc to throw spatter away from your nozzle.
          </p>
          <ul class="doc-bullet-list" style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
            <li>
              <strong><code class="mono">#1113</code> (<code class="mono">Ramp_lead_in_pn</code>):</strong> One-shot flag set before <code class="mono">M3</code> (<code class="mono">1.0</code> = arm 3D ramp; <code class="mono">0.0</code> = vertical plunge).
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong><code class="mono">#1110</code> (<code class="mono">Material_thickness_pn</code>):</strong> Tube wall or plate thickness used to choose a <code class="mono">60%</code> thin-sheet flying dwell or <code class="mono">100%</code> thick-wall dwell.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong><code class="mono">#2</code> (<code class="mono">Pierce_height</code>) &amp; <code class="mono">#3</code> (<code class="mono">Cut_height</code>):</strong> Program Z heights referenced as <code class="mono">Z#3</code> on your lead-in move.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 7 (Ramp Step 1)
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-7">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 07 • Ramp 1</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Define Handshake Parameters &amp; Material Thickness Fallback in <code class="mono">m3.py</code></h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              In <code class="mono">m3.py:145-183</code>, define both parameter numbers and <code class="mono">extract_thickness()</code>. That helper parses thickness from your SimCNC GUI cut chart if <code class="mono">#1110</code> is missing or if you selected thicker stock in the UI:
            </p>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot"></span> m3.py (Lines 145–183): Handshake Parameter Numbers</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">PYTHON</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>Ramp_lead_in_pn = 1113        # Set to 1.0 by RotaryCAM Post-Processor when 3D ramp lead-in is active
Material_thickness_pn = 1110  # Material thickness emitted by RotaryCAM Post-Processor</code></pre>
            </div>

            <p>
              <code class="mono">extract_thickness(text, unit)</code> converts gauges (<code class="mono">26 ga–7 ga</code>), metric strings (<code class="mono">mm</code>), fractions (<code class="mono">3/8</code>), or decimal inches into your active machine units (<code class="mono">inch</code> or <code class="mono">mm</code>).
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 8 (Ramp Step 2)
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-8">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 08 • Ramp 2</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Anchor Program Z to <code class="mono">Pierce_height (#2)</code> After Probing</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              After <code class="mono">m3.py:439-443</code> probes the surface (<code class="mono">touch_z</code>) and lifts to pierce height, set Program Z to <code class="mono">Pierce_height</code>:
            </p>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot cyan"></span> m3.py (Lines 439–443): Anchoring Program Z to Pierce_height (#2)</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">PYTHON</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>Pierce_height_position[Axis.Z.value] = touch_z + Pierce_height
d.moveToPosition(CoordMode.Machine, Pierce_height_position, Lifting_velocity)
d.setAxisProgPosition(Axis.Z, Pierce_height)</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="doc-callout info">
              <div class="doc-callout-title">🔬 Why You Anchor Program Z to Pierce_height (#2)</div>
              <p>
                Setting Program Z to <code class="mono">Pierce_height (#2)</code> puts the metal surface at <code class="mono">Program Z = 0.0</code>. When <code class="mono">m3.py</code> exits at <code class="mono">Pierce_height</code>, your next G-code block can command <code class="mono">Z#3</code> (<code class="mono">Cut_height</code>), and SimCNC interpolates the drop alongside X, Y, and A.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 9 (Ramp Step 3)
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-9">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 09 • Ramp 3</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Read the Ramp Flag (<code class="mono">#1113</code>) &amp; Resolve True Material Thickness</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Once <code class="mono">check_arc_ok(d)</code> confirms arc transfer, <code class="mono">m3.py:544-573</code> reads <code class="mono">#1113</code> and <code class="mono">#1110</code>:
            </p>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot"></span> m3.py (Lines 544–573): Reading #1113 &amp; #1110</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">PYTHON</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>try:
    ramp_lead_in_enabled = (float(d.getMachineParam(Ramp_lead_in_pn)) == 1.0)
except Exception:
    ramp_lead_in_enabled = False

try:
    Material_thickness = float(d.getMachineParam(Material_thickness_pn))
except Exception:
    Material_thickness = 0.0</code></pre>
            </div>

            <p>
              To avoid upward spatter blowout from moving too early on thick wall tube, <code class="mono">m3.py:555-573</code> checks <code class="mono">#1110</code> against <code class="mono">gui.edPlasmaMaterial.getText()</code> and takes <code class="mono">max(Material_thickness, gui_thickness)</code>. If <code class="mono">Pierce_delay &gt;= 700 ms</code> or <code class="mono">Pierce_height &gt;= 0.18"</code>, it defaults to <code class="mono">0.375"</code> / <code class="mono">9.5 mm</code>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 10 (Ramp Step 4)
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-10">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 10 • Ramp 4</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Implement Two-Tier Pierce Dwell (Flying Thin-Sheet vs. Full-Blowout Plate)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              In the pierce delay section (<code class="mono">m3.py:576-602</code>), branch your dwell time by wall thickness and delay:
            </p>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot emerald"></span> m3.py (Lines 576–602): Two-Tier Pierce Dwell Logic</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">PYTHON</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>if (Pierce_delay &gt; 0):
    thresh_thin = 0.080 if unit == "inch" else 2.0
    if ramp_lead_in_enabled and Material_thickness &lt;= thresh_thin and Pierce_delay &lt; 400.0:
        # Thin sheet (&lt;= 14 GA / ~0.080" / 2.0mm and short delay &lt; 400ms):
        # Flying ramp lead-in: reduce stationary dwell to 60% (min 100ms)
        ramp_dwell = max(100, int(Pierce_delay * 0.60))
        max_time = time.time() + (ramp_dwell / 1000.0)
        while max_time &gt; time.time():
            if not check_arc_ok(d):
                emergency("Torch went out while piercing")
            time.sleep(0.005)
    else:
        # Plate (&gt; 14 GA / &gt; 0.080" or Pierce delay &gt;= 400ms) or standard stationary pierce:
        # Full 100% nominal dwell at Pierce_height for complete puddle blowout
        max_time = time.time() + (Pierce_delay / 1000.0)
        while max_time &gt; time.time():
            if not check_arc_ok(d):
                emergency("Torch went out while piercing")
            time.sleep(0.005)</code></pre>
            </div>

            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>
                <strong>Tier 1 (Thin Sheet <code class="mono">&lt;= 0.080"</code> / <code class="mono">2.0 mm</code> &amp; <code class="mono">&lt; 400 ms</code> delay):</strong>
                Cuts stationary dwell to <code class="mono">60%</code> (min <code class="mono">100 ms</code>) so your diagonal XY+Z ramp launches on the fly.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>Tier 2 (Heavy Wall / Plate <code class="mono">&gt; 0.080"</code> / <code class="mono">2.0 mm</code> or <code class="mono">&gt;= 400 ms</code> delay):</strong>
                Holds <code class="mono">100% Pierce_delay</code> at <code class="mono">Pierce_height</code> for full blow-through, then ramps down to <code class="mono">Cut_height</code> while moving sideways out of rising slag.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 11 (Ramp Step 5)
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-11">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 11 • Ramp 5</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Skip Stationary Z Plunge &amp; Reset <code class="mono">#1113</code> at the End of <code class="mono">m3.py</code></h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              In the Move Cut Height block (<code class="mono">m3.py:604-616</code>), replace the stock unconditional plunge (<code class="mono">m3.py:200-205</code>) with this handoff:
            </p>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot cyan"></span> m3.py (Lines 604–616): Conditional 3D Ramp Handoff &amp; Flag Reset</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">PYTHON</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>if ramp_lead_in_enabled:
    print("  &gt;  3D Ramp Lead-In armed: Z remains at Pierce height for motion-synchronized ramp plunge")
    d.setMachineParam(Ramp_lead_in_pn, 0.0)  # Reset handoff flag
else:
    if (Pierce_height != Cut_height):
        print("  &gt;  Move Cut height")
        Cut_height_position = d.getPosition(CoordMode.Program)
        Cut_height_position[Axis.Z.value] = Cut_height
        d.moveToPosition(CoordMode.Program, Cut_height_position, Descent_velocity)
        print("  &gt;  Z axis on Cut height")</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="doc-callout tip">
              <div class="doc-callout-title">✓ Why #1113 Resets to 0.0 Inside m3.py</div>
              <p>
                Resetting <code class="mono">#1113 = 0.0</code> clears the flag after one pierce. If you run <code class="mono">M3</code> from MDI without setting <code class="mono">#1113=1</code>, <code class="mono">m3.py</code> falls back to a safe vertical drop to <code class="mono">Cut_height</code>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 12 (Ramp Step 6)
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-12">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 12 • Ramp 6</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Emit the Coordinated 3D Ramp Sequence in G-Code (RotaryCAM Post-Processor)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              With <strong>3D Ramp Lead-In (Flying Pierce)</strong> enabled, your posted G-code runs these three steps automatically:
            </p>
            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li>
                <strong>1. Check Lead-In Length:</strong> Your lead-in must be at least <code class="mono">minRampLeadLength</code> (<code class="mono">0.14"</code> / <code class="mono">3.5 mm</code>). Shorter lead-ins emit <code class="mono">#1113=0</code> so <code class="mono">m3.py</code> plunges vertically instead of diving too steep.
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>2. Arm <code class="mono">m3.py</code> &amp; Lock Hardware THC:</strong>
                <div class="doc-code-block">
                  <div class="doc-code-bar">
                    <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot"></span> RotaryCAM Post-Processor: Arming #1113 &amp; #1110 Before M03</span>
                    <span class="doc-code-lang">G-CODE</span>
                  </div>
                  <pre><code>#1113=1         ( Arm 3D ramp handoff in m3.py )
#1110=0.25      ( Pass material / wall thickness to m3.py )
M03             ( Probes, lifts to Pierce Height #2, fires, dwells, leaves Z at #2 )
M63 P0          ( Keep hardware THC locked during 3D ramp so high arc V at #2 cannot dive Z )</code></pre>
                </div>
              </li>
              <li>
                <strong>3. Execute 3D Linear or Helical Lead-In to <code class="mono">Z#3</code>:</strong>
                <div class="doc-code-block">
                  <div class="doc-code-bar">
                    <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot emerald"></span> RotaryCAM Post-Processor: 3D Linear &amp; Helical Arc Ramp Moves to Z#3</span>
                    <span class="doc-code-lang">G-CODE</span>
                  </div>
                  <pre><code>( Option A: 3D Linear Ramp Lead-In )
G01 X1.2500 Y0.8000 Z#3 F120.0

( Option B: 3D Helical Arc Ramp Lead-In )
G17 G03 X1.2500 Y0.8000 Z#3 I0.0000 J0.1500 F120.0

( Unlock Hardware THC once torch reaches Cut_height #3 on the cut contour )
M62 P0</code></pre>
                </div>
              </li>
            </ul>

            <p>
              SimCNC blends X, Y, Z, and rotary A together from <code class="mono">Z = #2</code> (<code class="mono">Pierce_height</code>) down to <code class="mono">Z = #3</code> (<code class="mono">Cut_height</code>). Right as your torch meets the contour, <code class="mono">M62 P0</code> unlocks hardware THC.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>
